    },
    "claim-2": {
      "summary": "The scheduler releases the GIL; the standard ZOS engine constructor selects its CPU data-parallel group, created with Gloo, and the scheduler's Gloo vote uses a CPU tensor. This is a constructor/code path observation, not proof that every scheduler branch avoids device synchronization.",
